Start the game at once: a plain launch goes straight to its loading screen, Steam and the build first.

Brighter Pocket carries one game. Opening the app showed Tolkara's library, where the player
tapped Brighter Shores every time; now a plain launch starts the library's default app by
itself, with the loading screen in front from the first frame (showStatusScreen, now a no-op
when it is in front already). The library still comes up when there is nothing to start: no
game found, or no execution mode chosen yet (once one is chosen, the game starts). The layer's
Steam sign-in and the game's update (launcher/Pocket/PocketSteamLaunch.m, PocketGameUpdates.m)
run first in libraryViewController:startApp:, before the start hashes and signs the executable:
an update changes it, and the page container must be the new build's (runNativeGame's own call
then finds the launch settled). Over the loading screen an alert would hide nothing behind it,
so a start that stops there says why on the loading screen, with Diagnostics. Preparing and
signing the game for this device show on it as well. Upstream candidate in a general form: a
setting to start the default app at launch; the Steam hook names this layer.

